#h1{Gaps for the assistant: hints and agents}

A literate program can be written with gaps. An author who knows what a chunk must do and has
not written it leaves a bag inside the chunk, `#agent-fill-in{what it must do}`, and an
assistant fills it in later with the whole document for context. This chapter is the first half:
finding the gaps, and the assistants that can be asked.

#hints: finding the gaps{
  A gap is a bag with the reserved tag `agent-fill-in`, written inside a chunk:
  `#agent-fill-in{count the words and print them}`. Tangle never emits it, so a program with gaps
  still tangles, and the gap is simply missing from the generated file. Finding the gaps walks the
  tree with offsets, because the editing that follows is done on the text and needs to know where
  each gap starts, at its hash, and where it ends, after its closing brace. Each site remembers
  its chunk, its words, its position in the text and its number among the gaps of the document.

  ```
  package lit

  import (
  	"fmt"
  	"strings"
  )

  // A HintSite is an #agent-fill-in{...} bag inside a chunk, with its place in the program text.
  type HintSite struct {
  	Index      int    // number among the hints of the program, in document order (the Index of the Hole)
  	Chunk      string // the chunk it sits in
  	Start, End int    // byte range of the whole bag in Source.Text
  	Text       string // the hint as plain text
  	Raw        string // the text between the braces, as written
  	File       string // source file (the root or a chapter) and the line in it
  	Line       int
  }

  // FindHints lists the hints of a program in document order. They are numbered exactly as Collect numbers its
  // holes, so site i and hole i are the same hint.
  func FindHints(src *Source, root Bag) []HintSite {
  	var out []HintSite
  	Walk(root, func(n Node, parents []Bag, start, end int) bool {
  		b, ok := n.(Bag)
  		if !ok {
  			return true
  		}
  		tag := strings.TrimSpace(b.Tag())
  		if b.Tag() == HintTag {
  			// a hint counts when every bag around it is a chunk (as in Collect) and there is one
  			for _, p := range parents[1:] {
  				if Reserved[strings.TrimSpace(p.Tag())] {
  					return false
  				}
  			}
  			if len(parents) < 2 {
  				return false
  			}
  			name, line, _ := src.Locate(start)
  			out = append(out, HintSite{Index: len(out), Chunk: strings.TrimSpace(parents[len(parents)-1].Tag()),
  				Start: start, End: end, Text: PlainText(b), Raw: src.Text[start+len(HintTag)+2 : end-1], File: name, Line: line})
  			return false
  		}
  		return !Reserved[tag]
  	})
  	return out
  }
  ```
}

